        {
          "name": "distribution",
          "type": "array",
          "description": "When using a weighted distribution, the value should be an array with a single item. For example: <pre>[\n  {\n    \"frequencies\": {\n      \"red\": \"1\",\n      \"green\": \"2\",\n      \"blue\": \"1\"\n    }\n  }\n]</pre> When using a dynamic distribution, each item should be an object with rule in Mockaroo formula syntax and frequencies. For example: <pre>[\n  {\n    \"rule\": \"gender == 'Male'\",\n    \"frequencies\": {\n      \"red\": \"1\",\n      \"green\": \"2\",\n      \"blue\": \"1\"\n    }\n  },\n  {\n    \"rule\": \"gender == 'Female'\",\n    \"frequencies\": {\n      \"red\": \"2\",\n      \"green\": \"1\",\n      \"blue\": \"1\"\n    }\n  }\n]</pre>",
          "default": null
        }
      ]
